/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Despite disruptions caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, stakeholder hesitancy, coordination delays, and resource limitations, the project sustained momentum through virtual engagements, tailored collaboration strategies, and strategic partnerships. Over time, institutional buy-in improved and several stakeholders adopted ACCA principles independently. The initiative resulted in long-term capacity-building, internal policy reform, curriculum integration in academic institutions, and regional and global visibility. The ACCA Working Group evolved into a self-sustaining platform, with members contributing to knowledge products and advancing ethical governance within their own institutions. The initiative has positioned GCNI as a national and international reference point for collective action against corruption, particularly in high-risk sectors like healthcare.)
/E (Despite disruptions caused by the COVID-19 pandemic, stakeholder hesitancy, coordination delays, and resource limitations, the project sustained momentum through virtual engagements, tailored collaboration strategies, and strategic partnerships. Over time, institutional buy-in improved and several stakeholders adopted ACCA principles independently. The initiative resulted in long-term capacity-building, internal policy reform, curriculum integration in academic institutions, and regional and global visibility. The ACCA Working Group evolved into a self-sustaining platform, with members contributing to knowledge products and advancing ethical governance within their own institutions. The initiative has positioned GCNI as a national and international reference point for collective action against corruption, particularly in high-risk sectors like healthcare.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
